Maven Research
1. What is Maven?
Maven is a build automation and dependency management tool used for Java and Spring Boot projects. It helps manage dependencies, compile code, run tests, and package applications.
2. pom.xml
pom.xml stands for Project Object Model. It is the main configuration file of a Maven project. It contains project information, dependencies, plugins, and build configuration.
3. Dependencies
Dependencies are external libraries required by a project. Maven downloads and manages these libraries automatically using the pom.xml file.
4. Plugins
Maven plugins are used to perform specific tasks such as compiling code, running tests, packaging the application, and running Spring Boot applications.
5. Repositories
Repositories are locations where Maven stores and downloads dependencies and plugins.
Main types:
•	Local Repository
•	Maven Central Repository
•	Remote Repository
6. Maven Lifecycle
The Maven lifecycle defines the steps used to build a project.
validate → compile → test → package → verify → install → deploy
7. Maven Commands
mvn clean
Removes the previous build output, usually the target folder.
mvn test
Compiles the test code and runs the project's tests.
mvn package
Builds the project and creates a packaged file such as a JAR.
mvn spring-boot
Runs a Spring Boot application using Maven.
8. Conclusion
Maven makes Java and Spring Boot development easier by managing dependencies, plugins, builds, testing, and application packaging through pom.xml.
